    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Planning</span>
    <h1>Best Time to Visit Hanoi by Motorbike</h1>
    <p>Hanoi has four real seasons, which is more than most of tropical Southeast Asia can say, and the season you choose changes the riding more than almost any other planning decision. The same city is a hot, bright, photo-friendly riding town in autumn, a steamy rain-management exercise in midsummer, and a cool, gray, atmospheric place in winter. This guide walks through the calendar honestly: what each period feels like on a bike, what it asks of your clothing and plans, and how to choose the window that matches the trip you want.</p>
    <p>The guide describes the general character of the seasons rather than inventing statistics, because specific temperatures and rainfall patterns belong to the forecast for your dates, which you should always check. It belongs to the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> hub, and it pairs with the two season-specific guides: the <a href="/motorbike-guides/riding-a-motorbike-in-hanoi-rainy-season/">rainy season guide</a> and the <a href="/motorbike-guides/riding-a-motorbike-in-hanoi-winter/">winter riding guide</a>.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
